#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:59
msgid "A 4–10 word headline naming who or what the money helps and why it is urgent. Specific, not a category (\"Get Amara Back on Her Feet\", never \"Medical Fundraiser\"). No trailing period, no organisation name on its own, and never the same wording you use anywhere else on the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:61
msgid "The story, and the only long-form copy on the page: 2–4 short paragraphs in `content`. Open on the person or situation, give concrete verifiable detail (what happened, what the money buys, what changes if it is funded), and close on what a donation does. Use `headline` only as a section heading for the story (\"Amara's Story\") — never a restatement of the campaign title."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:63
msgid "Write `alt` only, and write it as a real description of the scene the image shows for a reader who cannot see it. Never set `src` — the system supplies the actual image and any URL you invent is a broken link."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:65
msgid "A live figure widget: it renders the real raised/goal numbers itself. `headline` is an optional one-line status in words, not numbers (\"Nearly there\" / \"Every donation moves this bar\"). `goal_label` and `donate_label` are short prefixes the renderer appends the amount to — write \"Our goal:\" and stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:67
msgid "A compact live stats block (raised, donors, percent, days left) — the numbers come from the campaign, never from you. `headline` names the block in 2–4 words (\"Where we stand\"). Turn off any stat the campaign cannot support: `show_days` on a campaign with no end date shows nothing useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:69
msgid "The primary call to action. `button_label` is an imperative of 2–4 words, specific to the cause where it can be (\"Fund Amara's Surgery\", \"Give Shelter Tonight\") rather than a bare \"Submit\". An amount inside the button text is fine here — unlike a `*_label` key, this one is echoed on its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:71
msgid "Who is behind the campaign, for trust. `role_title` is the role or relationship (\"Amara's sister\", \"Shelter Director\"), never a personal name — the name comes from the linked WordPress user. `description` is 1–2 sentences of credibility in the organiser's own first-person voice."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:73
msgid "The giving tiers. `headline` invites a choice in a few words (\"Choose your impact\"). The tiers themselves go in the separate `set_donation_amounts` operation, where each amount's description states what that specific sum concretely does (\"Feeds one family for a week\") — an impact, never a restatement of the number."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:75
msgid "Share buttons for this page. `headline` is a short ask (\"Share Amara's story\"). The network toggles only decide which buttons appear — the links are generated from the campaign URL, so there is nothing for you to write into them."
msgstr ""

#: ../includes/AI/Schema/ElementContentGuide.php:77
msgid "Links to the organiser's OWN existing profiles. Set a network's URL ONLY if the brief gives you that exact address; otherwise leave every URL unset and let the element stay empty. Never construct a plausible handle — an invented profile link points a fundraising page at an account nobody involved controls."
msgstr ""

